        "original_id": "24018948-0690-5886-b4ad-97c0f5b2d697",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eli Manning, Peyton Manning, Archie Manning, David Tyree, Philip Rivers\n- Places: Manning Field at John L. Guidry Stadium\n- Organizations: New York Giants, San Diego Chargers, National Football League\n- Events: 2004 NFL Draft, Super Bowl XLII\n- Topics: Manning Passing Academy, Helmet Catch\n\nFacts:\n- Eli Manning was born on January 3, 1981, and he is an American football quarterback for the New York Giants of the National Football League.\n- In 2004, the San Diego Chargers drafted Eli Manning as the first overall pick in the 2004 NFL Draft and immediately traded him to the New York Giants in a deal highlighted by Philip Rivers, the fourth overall selection.\n- On February 3, 2008, the Helmet Catch was an American football play involving New York Giants quarterback Eli Manning and wide receiver David Tyree in the final two minutes of Super Bowl XLII.\n- Manning Field at John L. Guidry Stadium is named after the Manning family because Peyton Manning, Eli Manning, and Archie Manning hold the Manning Passing Academy football camp at the facility.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
